# The source manuscript is unpublished and belongs to its authors; it is not
# committed to this public repository.  Everything recovered from it that the
# code depends on is recorded in docs/ instead.
Discrimination2025*.pdf

# Simulation caches: regenerate with `python scripts/make_all.py --preset <p>`.
nn-based-simulation/data/
# Built by scripts/draft_comparison.py, and only meaningful next to the source PDF.
nn-based-simulation/figures/draft_comparison.pdf

# LaTeX build artefacts
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
# The paper's figures ARE committed, even though `make figures` regenerates them
# from nn-based-simulation.  They are small, and committing them means a coauthor who
# clones the repo and hits compile in an editor gets a paper, rather than fourteen
# missing-file errors and a hunt for the Makefile.  Do not add paper/figures/ here.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/

